| lr / schedule | 6e-4, cosine over all 129,173 steps, warmup 4% |
| max_grad_norm | 1.0 |
| num_anchors / loss_decay_gamma / objective_chunk_blocks | 512 / 7.0 / 128 |
| loss | 0.1 CE + 0.9 L1, confidence loss 0 |
| attention_backend | flex_attention |
| sharding / dtype / kernels | NO_SHARD (DDP) / bf16 / Liger |
| seed / prompt_seed | 42 / 42 |
| log_interval | 10 |

## Deployment (8x H200, `deployment.mode: disaggregated`, managed_local)

| | |
| --- | --- |
| capture servers | 2 x SGLang TP1 bf16 (`--spec-capture-method dspark`), GPUs 0-1, ports 30000-30001, `sglang_context_length` 8208, `max_running_requests` 4, `max_total_tokens` 65536, radix cache off, triton attention |
| trainer ranks | 6 x DDP, GPUs 2-7 |
| feature transport | Mooncake (tcp), 100 GiB segment, in-flight watermarks 396 / 528 samples (four optimizer quanta), resident 120 / 200 GiB |
| consumer dispatch | `cost_balanced` (PR #966): optimizer-window membership unchanged, microbatches assigned to ranks by estimated anchor/context cost; the profile showed ~24% of GPU time as ranks waiting for each other at the per-micro-step loss-denominator all-reduce |
| layout note | same GPU split as the dense arm. A 1-capture-GPU + 7-rank variant was tried (see the run log): one SGLang process cannot keep seven ranks fed (data wait 1.8 s/step, GPU 0 idle ~60% between prefill bursts), so the two-capture-GPU layout stays |
| launch | `WANDB_RUN_ID=dense-1-8 WANDB_RESUME=allow specforge train -c <yaml> model.target_model_path=/scratch/models/Qwen3-8B data.train_data_path=/scratch/data/perfectblend/...jsonl data.cache_dir=/scratch/cache/qwen3-8b-dspark-perfectblend-8192 output_dir=/scratch/outputs/<run_id> deployment.disaggregated.control_dir=/scratch/outputs/<run_id>/control tracking.wandb_dir=/scratch/outputs/<run_id>/wandb` |

Also on this branch: the `--nccl-port` pin for managed-local capture servers
(`specforge/launch_plan.py`), so two servers started in the same second cannot
collide on the torch.distributed TCPStore port.

## Continuation: epochs 13-18

At the user's request the run continues to 18 epochs. `deployment.managed_local` cannot resume a run, and the
12-epoch cosine schedule has decayed to 0, so epochs 13-18 are a separate launch on the same corpus and layout:

| | |
| --- | --- |
| start | weights-only warm start from the epoch-12 checkpoint (`<run_id>-step129168`); AdamW state is reset |
| LR schedule | 1% warmup to **2e-4** (1/3 of the original peak), cosine to 0 over the 6 epochs (64,586 steps) |
| prompt order | `training.prompt_seed: 54` (the first 12 epochs used 42) |
| run id / output | `qwen3-8b-dspark-dense-1-8-ep13-18`, checkpoint every 1,196 steps |
| W&B | the same run (`dense-1-8-r8`, `WANDB_RESUME=allow`) with `SPECFORGE_TRACKING_STEP_OFFSET=129168`, so the curve continues at step 129,168 = 12 x 10,764 instead of restarting; `train/segment_optimizer_step` holds the continuation's own step |
| launch | `launch_dense18.sh continue` (overrides on top of the recipe yaml); started automatically on the node once the 12-epoch run has finished cleanly |

Epoch 12+k is the continuation's step 10764*k checkpoint, listed below at global step 129168 + 10764*k. Expect a small
dip in train/acc right after epoch 12 while the LR warms up again.

